> Typically, home users have been subjected to very few, true performance NAS products[.] If you[ wanted true] performance[,] you had to[ reach a] little[ deeper into] your pocket, and pull[ out] a bit more of that hard earned money.
[With] Netgear being an industry leader in network storage solutions, it seems only fitting that they would[ offer top] to[ bottom] storage solutions[ for] every sector of the market. Today, on this crisp winter morning, we will be looking over the Netgear[ Ready]NAS 104. The RN104 is a four[ bay] NAS appliance that caters[ to the] needs[ of] consumers that[ want personal] cloud[ storage]. It[ offers standard] features[ like] a home media[ and file] server[,] coupled together[ with low] entry cost.
The RN104 is built upon the Marvell ARMADA 370 platform,[ cl]ocked at 1.2 GHz, with 512MB[ of] memory[ to] accompany it. Across the front of the unit, we[ have] four 3.5"[ drive] tr[ays] that[ support] tool[-less] installation[.] Total storage capacity is listed[ at] 16TB, with[ dual gig]abit LAN ports at the rear of the unit[.]
For[ quick] management of the NAS, we have a two line LCD screen on the front of the unit,[ with] dual[ USB] 3.0 ports, and e[S]ATA[ for additional storage] options[.] Power consumption is listed at 45 watts for operation, and 1.4 watts with WOL enabled.
